# What cannot be rebuilt: your corrections, and the ledgers of what was
# already researched, drafted and reported (core/storage.py), plus their
# daily backups. Personal, and this repo can be published.
data/
rejection_model.pkl
interview_model.pkl
followup_model.pkl
prep/
resumes/

# The filled-in resume: home address, EEO answers, salary expectations.
# resume_bank.example.json has the same shape with placeholders.
resume_bank.json

# Sheet snapshots taken before destructive edits — data, not code, and they
# carry the full application history including named contacts.
sheet-backup-*.csv

# Personal launchd agent: it hard-codes your home path.
# jobtracker.plist.example is the template.
com.*.jobtracker.plist
logs/draft_headers.json

# The sender's own identity: name, school, employer, contact details.
# profile.example.json has the same shape with placeholders.
profile.json

# A frozen pull of every confirmation email in the mailbox, used to measure
# the parser offline. Two years of one person's job search, and this repo is
# public. tests/test_confirmation_parser.py skips when it is absent.
tests/fixtures/confirmations.json

# What `pip install -e .` and `pip install .` leave behind.
*.egg-info/
build/

# --- Belt and braces -------------------------------------------------------
# The rules above name the files this project actually writes. These catch the
# same kinds of thing under a name nobody thought of: a scratch export, a
# second virtualenv, a database or spreadsheet dropped in the tree.
.venv/
env/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
people.db
*.csv
*.SKIPPED
out/
output/
exports/
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
*token*.json
.env.*
!.env.example
profile*.json
!profile.example.json
resume_bank*.json
!resume_bank.example.json
*.pkl
*.pickle
